# Everything listed here is excluded from the build context - the files Docker copies
# to the daemon before building. Two reasons this matters:
#
# 1. SECURITY: without this, "COPY . ." would bake .env (Atlas password, session secret,
#    Cloudinary secret, Mapbox token) into an image layer. Anyone who pulls the image can
#    read it with "docker history" even if a later layer deletes the file.
# 2. SPEED: node_modules and Notes/ are ~37MB+; sending them to the daemon on every build
#    is wasted time, and node_modules built on Windows may not even work in a Linux image.

# secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# installed inside the image by npm ci, never copied from the host
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# personal study notes, unrelated to the app
Notes

# docker's own files - not needed inside the image
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml

# kubernetes manifests
k8s

# editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# docs
README.md
